  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The trigonometric equation $\\sin ^{-1} x=2 \\sin ^{-1} 2 a$ has a real solution, if",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kVynW",
      "text": "$|a|>\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dJnxw",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}    < |a| < \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9bFbI",
      "text": "$|a|>\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MgQFS",
      "text": "$|a| \\leq \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that, $-\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\leq \\sin ^{-1} x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{-\\pi}{2} \\leq 2 \\sin ^{-1} 2 a \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{-\\pi}{4} \\leq \\sin ^{-1} 2 a \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin \\left(\\frac{-\\pi}{4}\\right) \\leq 2 a \\leq \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\leq 2 a \\leq \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{-1}{2 \\sqrt{2}} \\leq a \\leq \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}} \\Rightarrow|a| \\leq \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
